{"name":"Elevation","hex":"#b5ced5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elevation","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of raising from a lower place, condition, or quality to a higher; said of material things, persons, the mind, the voice, etc.","The condition of being or feeling elevated; heightened; exaltation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elevation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elevation","blocks":[{"text":"The elevation of a geographic location is its height above or below a fixed reference point, most commonly a reference geoid, a mathematical model of the Earth's sea level as an equipotential gravitational surface .\nThe term elevation is mainly used when referring to points on the Earth's surface, while altitude or geopotential height is used for points above the surface, such as an aircraft in flight or a spacecraft in orbit, and depth is used for points below the surface."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Vertical_distances.svg/330px-Vertical_distances.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elevation"},{"title":"Elevation (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Elevation is a 2024 American post-apocalyptic action thriller film directed by George Nolfi and written by Kenny Ryan and Jacob Roman. It stars Anthony Mackie, Morena Baccarin, and Maddie Hasson."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/51/Elevation_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elevation_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Satellite_image_of_Cape_peninsula.jpg/500px-Satellite_image_of_Cape_peninsula.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Satellite_image_of_Cape_peninsula.jpg/1280px-Satellite_image_of_Cape_peninsula.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Satellite_image_of_Cape_peninsula.jpg/500px-Satellite_image_of_Cape_peninsula.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Landsat Image over SRTM Elevation by NASA, showing the Cape Peninsula and Cape of Good Hope, South Africa in the foreground. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASatellite_image_of_Cape_peninsula.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Srtm_ramp2.world.21600x10800.jpg/500px-Srtm_ramp2.world.21600x10800.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Srtm_ramp2.world.21600x10800.jpg/1280px-Srtm_ramp2.world.21600x10800.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Srtm_ramp2.world.21600x10800.jpg/500px-Srtm_ramp2.world.21600x10800.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Heightmap of Earth's surface (including water and ice) in equirectangular projection, normalized as 8-bit grayscale, where lighter values indicate higher elevation.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASrtm_ramp2.world.21600x10800.jpg"}],"sounds":{"elevation":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/31/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-elevation.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/31/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-elevation.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-elevation.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/31/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-elevation.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-elevation.wav.